<Base title="Terms of service — Grossline">
  <h1>Terms of service</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated: 5 September 2026</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Grossline provides reporting on a merchant's own commerce and advertising data. Reports are
    prepared for the merchant they are addressed to and are not financial, tax or investment
    advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Access</h2>
  <p>
    Merchants grant Grossline read-only access to the platforms covered by their engagement. We
    never write to a merchant's store or ad accounts. Access can be revoked by the merchant at any
    time.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Numbers are computed from the data the platforms provide. Platforms restate historical data;
    reports reflect the data available at the time they were produced. Definitions used in reports
    are documented and applied consistently.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as-is. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Grossline's liability
    is limited to the fees paid for the month in which a claim arises.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:hello@getgrossline.com">hello@getgrossline.com</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
